summary: dump filesystem and path in /etc/kdump.conf
description: |
    This case is to configure local dump target in kdump.conf.

    Accepted Parameters:
     - MP:
       Mount point of dump device, defaulting to '/'. E.g. /mnt/data

     - KPATH:
       Specify 'path' in kdump.conf, defaulting to '/var/crash'.

     - OPTION:
       The valid are 'uuid', 'label' or 'softlink'.

     - LABEL:
       Only applicable when OPTION=label, specifying a label to the particular fs.

     - RAW:
       Value 'yes' means doing raw dump, default to 'no'.
contact: Kdump QE <kdump-qe-list@redhat.com>
test: chmod a+x ./runtest.sh; ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
require:
  - kexec-tools
duration: 30m
extra-summary: /kernel/kdump/config-fs
extra-task: /kernel/kdump/config-fs
